{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1538305-101-primal-families","id":1538305,"title":"101 Primal Families","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Curseborne"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-07-09T09:42:32-07:00","id":1538305,"title":"101 Primal Families","content":"Realized that with Primals there is a lot of wiggle room for transforming beings besides Werewolves, Werecats, Jekyll/Hydes, etc... <br /> <br /> Name of the game is to post a Family idea and continue the numbering on from the previous post/reply. Like so:<br /> <br /> 1. <b>Mantis </b>- Wild Form is chitinous with four arms.<br /> 2. <b>Fly </b>- Wild Form is an amalgamation of Fly and a Human like an H.R. Giger abomination.<br /> 3. <b>Socialite </b>- Wild Form is a extremely charismatic and suave, instead of getting the Physical boost it gets a Social boost, but the creature is about being seeing and any action that is not continuing a conversation or talking with people takes the penalty. (Think Steve Urkel's Stefan persona)<br /> 4. <b>Brainiac </b>- Wild form is a bulbious brain that requires constantly solving Mental tasks, the Creature needs knowledge and cannot help be addicted to mental challenges. Boost to Mental rolls instead of Physical, but gets penalties for not doing Mental actions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25291-donteatrawhagis","name":"DontEatRawHagis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-09T17:55:20-07:00","id":1538333,"title":"","content":"The fly ones sound terrifying<br /> I'm in","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-09T21:01:36-07:00","id":1538342,"title":"","content":"( Looks to his nWoD <b>Changing Breeds</b> love/hate book... ) Generally, whole Breeds from <b>CB</b> are great ideas for Families in <b>Curseborne</b>. Let's see...<br /> 5. <b>Ursus</b> - Bears. bears. BEARS. Did I say bears! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Majestic giants on day-to-day. Terrifying beasts in rage. Especially in 'rage on G town'. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Even have Family photo. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Great healers by lore. Like to travel in their own company, even in fantasy games<a href=\"https://www.pcgamer.com/pillars-of-eternity-diary-playing-as-a-party-of-bears/\" target=\"_blank\">.</a> ( Half joke, half serious - I'm one of them, in real life. Had one Werebear Gay Healer NPC in my <b>Werewolf</b> game around year 2014. Good times. )<br /> <br /> <img data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://www.starobserver.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2018/04/ann-marie-calilhanna-hcb-launch-night-@-kinselas_112.jpeg\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://www.starobserver.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2018/04/ann-marie-calilhanna-hcb-launch-night-@-kinselas_112.jpeg\" data-thumb-url=\"https://www.starobserver.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2018/04/ann-marie-calilhanna-hcb-launch-night-@-kinselas_112.jpeg\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> 6. <b>Cold Blooded (Royality)</b> - Dinosaurs changers. No, really. You are descendant of ancient FAMILY, stretching time even before humanity itself. Now you are somehow forgotten nobility of reptiles.<br /> 7. <b>Titans</b> - Elephant. Whales. Your Beast is one of biggest animals in the world. Be afraid of those who get in your way.<br /> 8. <b>Strangers</b> - Rodent shifters. Rats laughing in dark corners, treating people from the belly up as Swarm Form. Mouse shifters that can with their teeth almost anything. Hamsters that... well, that can eat in their hybrid form. A LOT. Human or two at least.<br /> 9. <b>Apes</b> - You are human... not quite. Offshoot of some evolutionary last branch on <b>Homininae</b> FAMILY tree. You are powerful - but also unnerving, in Uncanny Valley way for humans.<br /> 10. <b>Runners</b> - Deer-, elk-, horse- and a like folk. Always in the hurry. Always watch out in the woods - or they will stomp you - to the death....<br /> 11. <b>Spinners</b> (<b>Eight Hands</b> are canon Spiders Family, so simply miss this entry) - Spiders folk. Most often Swarm form, but in War-Beast form, these beings appear as luminous spiders standing nearly six feet tall at the shoulder. Watch out for their webs - of intrigue - and literal, in their basements...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 07-10-2024, 02:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"