s://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-19T06:02:47-07:00","id":1538897,"title":"","content":"12. <b>Shining Tusks</b> - Suids. Boisterous, brash, tough as hell, your best friends or your worst enemies; most of all <i>all</i> about family.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Lead Writer for the Savage Age of Werewolf: the Apocalypse: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/428750/Ghost-Lineages-The-Advanced-Players-Guide-to-the-Savage-Age\" target=\"_blank\">Ghost Lineages</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/312700/The-Rise-of-the-Garou-The-Savage-Age-Volume-Two\" target=\"_blank\">Rise of the Garou</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/331302/Tools-of-Extinction-The-Savage-Age-Volume-Three\" target=\"_blank\">Tools of Extinction</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/352717/Tribebook-Wlewa\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook: Wlewa</a>.<br /> <br /> Want RPGs in libraries? Check out my book, <a href=\"http://www.abc-clio.com/ABC-CLIOCorporate/product.aspx?pc=A3951P\" target=\"_blank\">Dragons in the Stacks</a>. Now with <a href=\"http://www.ennie-awards.com/blog/2015-ennie-award-nominees-and-spotlight-winners/\" target=\"_blank\">awards</a>!<br /> \u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1813-grimjaws","name":"grimjaws","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1813_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-23T10:45:40-07:00","id":1539105,"title":"","content":"Okay! Now that we know Creatures are defined by a desire for safety at all costs and something else...<br /> <br /> <b>13. Arboreals: </b>The source (or drawn from?) the legend of tricksy wood nymphs and related entities like huldras, Arboreals are were-trees and other plants. Sounds funny, until you realize how murderously competitive and patient plants are. Arboreals are born of a type of Creature that desires control over themselves and their immediate environs, and to reshape it into a perfect home - and don't mind watering the plants with blood and feeding them fertilizer now and again. That being said, they're insular and aloof, not cruel; an Arboreal enjoys &quot;symbiotes&quot; in their groves to help them thrive, and are often middle-managers and messengers for other families...and master trappers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-24T04:07:52-07:00","id":1539138,"title":"","content":"For those wanting to dwell deeper into story and lore of Primsls for creating Families of them - <b><a href=\"https://theonyxpath.com/curseborne-the-primal-1/\" target=\"_blank\">we have official blog post on Primals</a> and example Family of Get of Lyka! \ud83d\ude32</b><br /> <br /> Two thougts from blog post:<br /> 1. Each Animal changer is also connected to elements. Get of Lyka, werewolves - are connected to Lighting! \ud83d\ude32 ( <b>WtF</b> <b><i>Storm Lords</i></b> are coming! \u2764\ufe0f<br /> 2. Each Primal Family is <b><i>very</i></b> broad - 'Lykans' are also <i>'Pinscher dogs, foxes, jackals, or coyotes'</i> changers. \ud83d\ude32<br /> <br /> <br /> P.S.<i> 'Izzy Plummer is a werewolf from the Get of Lyka. She shortens their <b>name to \u201cLykans.\u201d'</b> </i><br /> I see what you did here. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> But truly - I need to take out my <b>WtF</b> 2E core and re-read info on Lycon-Ur! \ud83d\udc3a<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <img width=\"1425\" height=\"1425\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.pinimg.com/originals/df/ce/98/dfce98ceb43e31e76538d61dffe577a7.jpg\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.pinimg.com/originals/df/ce/98/dfce98ceb43e31e76538d61dffe577a7.jpg\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.pinimg.com/originals/df/ce/98/dfce98ceb43e31e76538d61dffe577a7.jpg\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 07-24-2024, 10:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-25T10:22:56-07:00","id":1539225,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://theonyxpath.com/curseborne-the-primal-2/\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Blog post about <i>Hydes</i> Primal Family</b></a> - for inspiration to you all. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-26T03:51:28-07:00","id":1539302,"title":"","content":"All the worlds for packs, flocks, herds, etc. in English - for your animal families. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/shorts/-I15FAG0nlo\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/shorts/-I15FAG0nlo\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/shorts/-I15FAG0nlo\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/shorts/-I15FAG0nlo </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-27T19:17:36-07:00","id":1539404,"title":"","content":"<b>14. The Horologians: </b>A Family only slightly older than the Hydes, the Horologians are unique in that their Creatures aren't animals - or anything organic at all. They are spirits of metal and machines, originally clocks (as the name suggests), but as tech advanced, so have the Wild Forms of the Horologians - the majority of modern ones look like sleek cyborgs and humanoid war machines in their battle forms, though there has been a callback to steam(punk) tech. Their founder wanted them to be the best of human and machine, the passion of a human with the ruthless efficiency of technology - this backfired, as the Creatures of Horologians are just as proud and paranoid as their more organic counterparts, they just combine that with a more slow, logic-driven burn to their ire that lets them plan out (and draw out) their inevitable retaliation. The urge of a Horologian Creature is control - for everything around them to proceed to according to predictable, clockwork cycles of stability, and a fundamental part of that is understanding the world - and justice, to ensure the correction fits the pattern. Hell hath no fury like a Clockwork who both personally hates you and has a law or moral principle to cite for justification.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","user":"Leliel","date":". 07-28-2024, 01:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-01T10:25:47-07:00","id":1539643,"title":"","content":"On latest blog post we have Primals - Spawn of Vodnik, my Eastern Europe countrymans! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><b><a href=\"http://%C2%A0https://theonyxpath.com/curseborne-the-primal-3/\" target=\"_blank\"> https://theonyxpath.com/curseborne-the-primal-3/</a></b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 08-01-2024, 03:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-12T06:28:46-07:00","i